> Cross-tracking: [GitCode #101](https://gitcode.com/openJiuwen/sciencediscovery/issues/101) (Chinese counterpart of this issue).

### 🚀 Background Description

ScienceDiscovery already surfaces failures to the user — connection errors, 401/5xx request failures, settings save errors, panel render crashes, and Run/tool execution errors — via toasts, inline alerts, panel error boundaries, and Run summary text. Those surfaces currently offer only **Dismiss / Retry**. There is **no** way to copy the diagnostics that belong to that error, and **no** way to turn it into an issue from the same place.

What users actually have to do today:

1. The UI shows a short message such as `Request error: Unauthorized` or a panel `render failed`;
2. The useful evidence lives in rolling files under the data directory (default `.sciencediscovery-data/logs/` — `api.log`, `runner.log`, `run.log`). Many users do not know where that is or which slice to attach;
3. They leave the product, open GitCode or GitHub, fill a template by hand, and must remember to redact tokens, API keys, and session content.

Real failures therefore rarely become actionable issues. Maintainers get “it errored” without version, error code, run/request ids, or nearby log lines.

This request is a **user-facing feedback mechanism**, not another developer-only log sink. It complements the framework diagnostic-logging work ([GitHub #8](https://github.com/openJiuwen-ai/sciencediscovery/issues/8), GitCode [#74](https://gitcode.com/openJiuwen/sciencediscovery/issues/74)): #8/#74 explicitly **do not** add a log viewer, search, or download UI. This issue is the missing “copy key logs + file an issue” path at the error itself.

### Design Ideas

On **user-visible errors**, add two actions (copy can be refined):

1. **Copy key diagnostics**: write a redacted, size-capped bundle to the clipboard. At minimum:
   - product version / build id;
   - OS and UI locale;
   - error title and body;
   - request / run / session ids when they exist;
   - the last few service-log lines related to this failure (reuse the redaction and length caps from #8/#74; do not copy whole log files).
2. **File an issue**: open the repository’s new-issue page with title and body prefilled from that bundle. GitCode (`openJiuwen/sciencediscovery`) is the canonical tracker; GitHub (`openJiuwen-ai/sciencediscovery`) is the public mirror — offer a GitHub link or a locale-based choice. The product must **not** create the issue on the user’s behalf and must **not** upload logs to a third party.

Priority error surfaces (can ship incrementally via one shared control):

- error toasts (`apps/web/src/Toasts.tsx` — dismiss only today);
- inline settings/dialog alerts (`apps/web/src/InlineErrorAlert.tsx` — dismiss only today);
- panel error boundaries (`apps/web/src/ErrorBoundary.tsx` — `label` + `message` only today);
- user-visible Run / tool failure text;
- CLI failures that have no equivalent Web surface.

**Alternatives considered**

- Copy-only, no “file issue” action: users still have to find the repo and the template.
- In-app form posting to a private backend: extra infra and auth, out of scope.
- Dumping full log files or unredacted session / tool payloads: leaks tokens, API keys, and research content.
- Silent crash telemetry: not part of this request.

**Open questions (need a product decision before implementation)**

- Whether “File an issue” defaults to GitCode or chooses GitCode vs GitHub from the UI locale;
- Whether the bundle is assembled in the client from the already-visible error plus version info, or via a local authenticated snapshot API (unredacted log files must not be exposed over HTTP).

### Involved Public APIs

- **User-visible behavior**: add Copy / File-issue actions on error controls; do not change the meaning of existing error copy.
- **HTTP**: if the client cannot see nearby log lines, a local authenticated read-only snapshot endpoint may return the redacted fields above. Do not expose `.sciencediscovery-data/logs/` as downloadable files, and do not add an anonymous public log download.
- **Issue hosts**: only open the public GitCode / GitHub “new issue” pages with prefilled content. Do not call their write APIs and do not embed a full issue editor.

### Description of Relevance to Other Modules

- Web error UI: toasts, inline alerts, error boundaries, Run summaries;
- `packages/operational-logging` and [GitHub #8](https://github.com/openJiuwen-ai/sciencediscovery/issues/8) / [GitCode #74](https://gitcode.com/openJiuwen/sciencediscovery/issues/74): reuse existing redaction, rotation, and size caps;
- CLI: the same class of failure should yield a copyable diagnostics block;
- This does not replace the framework-internal events in #8/#74, and must not put user prompts, model I/O, or tool arguments/results into the bundle.

### Test Design and Test Plan

**Functional**

- [ ] Error toast, inline alert, and error boundary expose “Copy key diagnostics” in the failure state; the clipboard contains version + error body and does **not** contain access tokens / API keys / Bearer values;
- [ ] “File an issue” opens a new-issue URL for `openJiuwen/sciencediscovery` (and optionally the GitHub mirror) with title/body already carrying the error summary and diagnostics bundle;
- [ ] Dismissing the error does not upload logs or create an issue in the background;
- [ ] CLI user-visible failures print or otherwise provide an equivalent copyable diagnostics block (if CLI is in this slice).

**Security**

- [ ] The bundle uses the same redaction as #8/#74 (Authorization/Bearer, token, secret, password, cookie, URL userinfo);
- [ ] User prompts, tool arguments/results, and full stdout/stderr files are absent;
- [ ] Log excerpts and oversized error messages are truncated to an explicit cap.

**Engineering / user journey**

- [ ] Focused unit tests and Web control tests pass;
- [ ] User-journey E2E: induce a visible error → copy → assert clipboard → assert the “file issue” link opens with a complete prefilled body. Formal E2E must not use the human trial port 4310 or its fixed data directory.

### Additional Information

Code pointers (repo-relative, for implementers; not the acceptance surface):

- `apps/web/src/Toasts.tsx`
- `apps/web/src/InlineErrorAlert.tsx`
- `apps/web/src/ErrorBoundary.tsx`
- `apps/web/src/App.tsx` (request errors go to the top-right toast)
- Data-directory logs: `.sciencediscovery-data/logs/` (`api.log` / `runner.log` / `run.log`)
